thub.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/4243441312", "html_url": "https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/7005#issuecomment-4243441312", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/7005", "id": 4243441312, "node_id": "IC_kwDOPRF1G8787cag", "user": {"login": "audanye-sudo", "id": 228663729, "node_id": "U_kgDODaEhsQ", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228663729?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo", "html_url": "https://github.com/audanye-sudo", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/audanye-sudo/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-04-14T11:15:33Z", "updated_at": "2026-04-14T11:15:33Z", "body": "For anyone still hitting this \u2014 the root causes are now addressed in three PRs:\n\n- **#9609** fixes the async bugs and message parsing issues mentioned in the last comment (and referenced in #5037). The `dingtalk.py` code was reading fields from the wrong object layer and had broken async handling.\n- **#9608** fixes the webhook domain validation \u2014 `oapi.dingtalk.com` was being rejected, so replies never went out even if messages were received.\n- **#9610** adds a QR code scan option to the DingTalk setup wizard, plus auto-detection of `DINGTALK_CLIENT_ID` / `DINGTALK_CLIENT_SECRET` env vars in `gateway/config.py` \u2014 so you don't necessarily need the yaml config block if you have the env vars set.\n\nThe yaml config approach mentioned by @HongHaiyang is correct and still works, but with #9610 merged, env vars alone would also enable the platform automatically.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/4243441312/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]